==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-back into.ogg|a=AU}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|*}}

# {{lb|en|sports|idiomatic}} To [[advance]] to the [[post-season]] as a result of another [[team]]'s [[loss]], especially where one's own team has also lost.
#: {{ux|en|The 2006 St. Louis Cardinals '''backed into''' the playoffs.}}
# {{lb|en|sports|idiomatic}} To be forced into a situation by circumstances.
#: {{ux|en|I didn't have any other options, I was '''backed into''' it.}}
# {{&lit|en|back|into}}
#: {{ux|en|I like to '''back into''' parking spots.}}

